<H2><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Humor">Humor</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Humor" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran&amp;action=3D=
edit&amp;section=3D33">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H2>
<P>During the same Fortran standards committee meeting at which the name =

"FORTRAN 77" was chosen, a satirical technical proposal was incorporated =
into=20
the official distribution bearing the title, "Letter O <A =
title=3D"Considered harmful"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Considered_harmful">considered =
harmful</A>".=20
This proposal purported to address the confusion that sometimes arises =
between=20
the letter "O" and the numeral zero, by eliminating the letter from =
allowable=20
variable names. However, the method proposed was to eliminate the letter =
from=20
the character set entirely (thereby retaining 48 as the number of =
lexical=20
characters, which the colon had increased to 49). This was considered =
beneficial=20
in that it would promote structured programming, by making it impossible =
to use=20
the notorious <CODE><B>GO TO</B></CODE> statement as before. =
(Troublesome=20
<CODE><B>FORMAT</B></CODE> statements would also be eliminated.) It was =
noted=20
that this "might invalidate some existing programs" but that most of =
these=20
"probably were non-conforming, anyway".<SUP class=3D"reference"=20
id=3D"cite_ref-37"><A=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran#cite_note-37"><SPAN>[</SPAN=
>37<SPAN>]</SPAN></A></SUP><SUP=20
class=3D"reference" id=3D"cite_ref-38"><A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran#cite_note-38"><SPAN>[</SPAN=
>38<SPAN>]</SPAN></A></SUP></P>
<P>During the standards committee battle over whether the "minimum trip =
count"=20
for the FORTRAN 77 <CODE><B>DO</B></CODE> statement should be zero =
(allowing no=20
execution of the block) or one (the "plunge-ahead" =
<CODE><B>DO</B></CODE>),=20
another facetious alternative was proposed (by Loren Meissner) to have =
the=20
minimum trip be two=E2=80=94since there is no need for a loop if it is =
only executed=20
once.<SUP class=3D"noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" =
style=3D"white-space: nowrap;">[<I><A=20
title=3D"Wikipedia:Citation needed" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed"><SPAN=20
title=3D"This claim needs references to reliable sources. (January =
2015)">citation=20
needed</SPAN></A></I>]</SUP></P>
<P>When assumed-length arrays were being added, there was a dispute as =
to the=20
appropriate character to separate upper and lower bounds. In a comment =
examining=20
these arguments, Dr. Walt Brainerd penned an article entitled, =
"Astronomy vs.=20
Gastroenterology" because some proponents had suggested using the star =
or=20
asterisk ("*"), while others favored the colon (":").</P>
